md`. `realpath` from `plugins/development-harness/docs/` resolves to the real repo-root file; confirmed present. |\n\n**8 of 9 criteria fully MET, 1 PARTIAL (AC #6).**\n\n### AC #6 re-verification (evidence chain)\n\n1. `git show --stat fadeacc1d` \u2192 5 files changed:\n   - `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` (the target doc \u2014 in scope)\n   - `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json`\n   - `plugins/development-harness/.codex-plugin/plugin.json`\n   - `plugins/development-harness/.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`\n   - `.claude/agent-memory/dh-service-docs-maintainer/MEMORY.md`\n2. The 3 `plugin.json` files are version-bump-only diffs (`git show fadeacc1d -- '*.plugin/plugin.json'` \u2192 single-line version field change each), matching the pattern the amendment exempts. **Covered by the amendment \u2014 no violation.**\n3. `MEMORY.md` gained a 4-line note (\"Worktree isolation: when cwd is under `.claude/worktrees/...`\") recording an operational lesson the `service-docs-maintainer` agent learned while doing the T5 remediation. This is the platform's built-in Persistent Agent Memory feature (`memory: project` frontmatter, `.claude/agent-memory/`), explicitly designed to be \"shared with your team via version control\" per the agent's own instructions \u2014 not a manifest bump, and **not named by the amendment's exemption text**, which reads: *\"version-bump-only edits to `plugin.json` manifests made automatically by the repo's `auto-sync-manifests` pre-commit hook... are exempted\"*. A memory-file write is agent-authored, not hook-generated, so it falls outside the literal exemption.\n4. **Discrepancy in the item's own confirmatory text**: the amended AC #6 asserts \"The landed commit (`fadeacc1d`...) touches exactly one content file plus these automated manifest bumps.\" Direct evidence (`git show --stat fadeacc1d`) shows it touches **two** non-manifest files (the doc and `MEMORY.md`), not one. This assertion should be corrected regardless of the ultimate policy call on `MEMORY.md`.\n\n**Judgment call**: This is a materially different, much lower-risk situation than the original AC #6 finding \u2014 `MEMORY.md` is agent tooling infrastructure (not user-facing doc content, not a functional file, versioned by platform design), and the same rationale the amendment already accepted for the manifest hook (\"deterministic repo automation... not agent-introduced scope creep\") plausibly extends to it. However, the amendment's text does not say so explicitly, and per this SOP's evidentiary bar I cannot silently extend an exemption whose wording doesn't cover the file I found. Marking PARTIAL rather than UNMET reflects that the criterion's substantive purpose (no unrelated *functional* content sneaking into the doc fix) is intact \u2014 only a wording/scope-boundary question remains.\n\n**Fastest remediation** (either one closes this cleanly):\n- (a) Broaden AC #6's exemption wording to also cover `.claude/agent-memory/**` writes made by the executing agent's platform-mandated persistent-memory feature, alongside the existing `plugin.json` exemption; or\n- (b) Amend the confirmatory sentence to accurately state file count and explicitly bless the memory-file write with the same rationale already applied to the manifest bumps.\n\nNo code or doc-content change is required \u2014 this is a scope-gate wording/confirmation-text issue only.\n\n---\n\n## T2 gap resolution (verified, not part of the 9 ACs but in the same reviewed diff)\n\nT2 (feature-verifier) previously flagged: `:5` cited a non-existent API, `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)`. `backlog_core/server.py` has no such parameter.\n\n`fadeacc1d`'s diff on the doc corrects this to `backlog_groom(selector=..., section=..., content=...)` (`backlog_core/server.py:2550`). Verified directly: `sed -n '2545,2551p' backlog_core/server.py` shows `async def backlog_groom(ctx: Context, selector: ..., ...)` at line 2550 \u2014 the citation and the signature both check out. **Gap resolved, confirmed independently.**\n\n---\n\n## Universal Findings\n\nPure prose/documentation change \u2014 most universal dimensions (security, tests, API contracts other\nthan the one above, error handling, performance) are not applicable.\n\n### Blocking (Required Changes)\n\n- **[CONTRACT]** Backlog item #3332, Acceptance Criteria section, AC #6's confirmatory text \u2014 states the remediation commit `fadeacc1d` \"touches exactly one content file plus these automated manifest bumps,\" which is inaccurate (it touches two non-manifest files: the target doc and `.claude/agent-memory/dh-service-docs-maintainer/MEMORY.md`). Required change: correct the AC #6 text to reflect the actual file set, and either explicitly extend the scope-gate exemption to platform-mandated agent-memory writes or split the memory-file update into a change not attributed to this item's commit.\n\n### Non-Blocking (Recommendations)\n\n- None \u2014 the doc content itself (all six original text corrections plus the T5 API-citation fix) is textually and semantically correct, verified independently against `backlog_core/models.py`'s live vocabulary constants, `AGENTS.md`'s Backend Providers section, `research/README.md`'s existence, and `backlog_core/server.py`'s actual `backlog_groom` signature.\n\n---\n\n## Stack-Specific Findings\n\nNo stack skill applied (plain documentation, no frontmatter/skill/agent structure matching the `dh:code-review-*` detection table).\n\n### Blocking\n\nNone.\n\n### Non-Blocking\n\nNone.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**Files reviewed:** 1 target file (`plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`) + 4 incidentally-touched files across the reviewed commits (3 manifests, 1 agent-memory file) + primary sources (`backlog_core/models.py`, `backlog_core/server.py`, `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md`, `research/README.md`)\n**Acceptance criteria:** 8/9 fully MET, 1/9 PARTIAL\n**Blocking findings:** 1 (AC #6 confirmatory-text/scope-wording gap)\n**Non-blocking findings:** 0\n\nAll nine acceptance criteria's substantive intent is satisfied: the frontmatter, storage framing,\nstatus vocabulary, priority vocabulary, `title`/`name` prose rule, and research link are all\nindependently verified correct against primary sources, and the previously-outstanding T2 gap (a\nfalse `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)` API citation) has been fixed and independently confirmed\nagainst the real function signature. The sole remaining issue is narrow and specific to AC #6: the\n2026-08-31 amendment correctly resolves the original manifest-bump violation, but the very\nremediation commit that fixed the T2 gap (`fadeacc1d`) also wrote a 4-line note to an agent's\npersistent-memory file \u2014 a file type the amendment's exemption wording does not name, and one the\nitem's own confirmatory text incorrectly claims doesn't exist. This is materially lower-risk than\nthe original finding (internal agent tooling infrastructure, not doc content), and is a\none-sentence wording fix away from full PASS, but per this review's evidentiary standard it cannot\nbe waved through silently. Verdict is FAIL strictly on this narrow AC #6 residual; no further edit\nto the reviewed doc is required.\n"}